  "details": "YES I KNOW THE CONTROLLERS DO THIS ANYWAYS, but still\n\nAs we all know you can calibrate the index controllers via drumming your fingers across the pad Or squeezing and letting go of the grip multiple times.\n\nUnfortunately, everybody’s hands are different and they won’t always calibrate perfectly with the controllers even if they are in great condition\n\nAbility to manually calibrate your index controller finger roll, inside of the game to allow you freely move your fingers with more accurate tracking. This will work similar to how full body tracking calibration works except that it will require you to do finger poses and set the value for your current finger position. Doing this once and then saving it allow you to apply every time you boot up the game without having to recalibrate every time unless you want to.\n\nThis doesn’t take account for adjusting your hand position, but it will give you a better tracking overall for your fingers that will not rotate correctly with the controller in it’s normal state, also since Valve nor any other software exists for this, it will be a great feature for those with or without index finger tracking difficulty.\n\n(yes, this suggestion was based on your controller being in good condition, If your controller is broken, then there’s a high chance the calibration won’t work)\n\nCalibration Saved!!!!",
